From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] make shared blackbody object wait for generated colour tables

The original rule declares the generated include prerequisites only for the
static blackbody.o. Under make -j2 the .c.lo suffix rule can compile the shared
blackbody.lo before 10deg-rgb.i exists. Package CI 39173536316/1 fails at
blackbody.c:26 with that missing include after a successful dependency install.

Give both objects the same existing generated-input and header prerequisites.
Keep the original all target, target-built generator, full table data, compiler
commands, parallelism, library contents and functional consumers unchanged.
This is a portable build-graph defect, not a RISC-V code change.

License: ISC (same as upstream Makefile).
Upstream status: downstream-only; no upstream write.
Remove when a fixed official source declares these shared-object prerequisites.
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 all: libred.a libred.$(LIBEXT)
 solar.o: libred.h
-blackbody.o: 10deg-xy.i 10deg-rgb.i libred.h
+blackbody.o blackbody.lo: 10deg-xy.i 10deg-rgb.i libred.h
 generate-table.o: blackbody.c 10deg-xy.i libred.h
 
 10deg-xy.i: 10deg
